{"text": "LISA HERBOLD\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nJanuary 2016 -\nCurrent\n\nJanuary 1998 \u2014\nDecember 2015\n\nMay 1997 \u2014\nNovember 1997\n\nSpring 1993 \u2014 May\n1997\n\nSummer 1992 \u2014\nSpring 1993\n\nFall 1989 \u2014\nSummer 1992\n\nSpring 1989 \u2014 Fall\n1989\n\nVOLUNTEER\n\nBoard of Directors\n\nEDUCATION\n\n1984-1989\n\nCity Councilmember, District 1, West Seattle and South Park, City of Seattle\n\n+ Helped craft and pass public policy that includes Paid Sick Leave for the 190,000 Seattle\nworkers who didn\u2019t have it, a Rental Housing Inspection Program for 250,000 renter\nhouseholds, and the pilot project for LEAD, an acclaimed criminal justice diversion program.\n\nLegislative Aide, The Office Of Councilmember Nick Licata, City Council, City of Seattle\n+ Policy analysis, development, and implementation, project management, constituent\nand press relations, annual newsletter editor, and scheduling.\n\nCampaign Coordinator, People for Nick Licata\n\n+ Responsible for coordination of all aspects of campaign, from volunteer recruitment and\nsupervision, event planning, press relations, strategy and tactics, and materials\ndevelopment.\n\nTenant Organizer, Seattle Tenants\u2019 Union\n\n+ Staffed a statewide tenants\u2019 rights hotline, conducted trainings for advocacy organizations\non tenants\u2019 rights, bringing groups of tenants together in their buildings towards collective\naction on issues of common concern whether focused upon changes to their individual\ntenancy or towards larger policy changes.\n\nLead Organizer, Association for Community Organization for Reform Now (ACORN)\n\n+ Managed, with the Head Organizer, all aspects of launching a new Seattle office and from\nthe ground up, building a staff, organizational infrastructure, and a membership base where\nthere had been none.\n\nSouthside Organizer, Syracuse United Neighbors (SUN)\n\n+ Responsible for managing membership group of 400 individuals, monthly and bi-monthly\nmeetings, as well as neighborhood issue-based campaigns, including press relations and\nleadership development.\n\nCanvass Director, Syracuse New York Public Interest Research Group (NYPIRG)\n\n+ Hired, trained, and supervised canvassing staff of ~ 20 as well as managing all aspects of the\nsummer canvass, from maintaining financial records, on-going reporting to State\nheadquarters, to managing the day-to-day operations of a busy office.\n\nHomestead Community Land Trust (1997 - 1999), Young Adult Independent Living\nProgram (1998 \u2014 2000), Neighborhood House 2004-2006, The Tenants Union 2006 \u2014\n2010\n\nSyracuse University, Political Science/Journalism",
